      "content": "i mean i get the middle ground thing, but it feels like one side has way more actual evidence. like, aren't most experts saying that keeping things single-family is basically just a way to keep prices high and stop progress? it feels like the \"neighborhood character\" argument is just a way to avoid the real solution of building more density.",
